# Exercises every Payment endpoint against the compose stack (`docker compose up -d --build`).
# Run the requests top to bottom in the IntelliJ HTTP client; the token requests store tokens for
# the ones after them. Each change also publishes a payment.payment event; the README shows how to
# watch the topic.

@payment = http://localhost:8084
@keycloak = http://localhost:8180/realms/ecomm/protocol/openid-connect/token
@userinfo = http://localhost:8180/realms/ecomm/protocol/openid-connect/userinfo
@gateway = http://localhost:8000/api/payment

### Customer token
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=dev-cli&username=demo@ecomm.local&password=demo&scope=openid

> {% client.global.set("customerToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### The demo Customer's ID: the sub the checkout Saga names in the body
GET {{userinfo}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

> {% client.global.set("customerId", response.body.sub); %}

### Orchestration token: the checkout Saga's own identity, for the commands it calls
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id=orchestration&client_secret=orchestration-dev-secret

> {% client.global.set("orchestrationToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### The checkout Saga authorizes an Order's payment for the Customer: 201, AUTHORIZED by the approving test card, with its AUTHORIZATION transaction
< {% client.global.set("authorizeKey", $random.uuid); %}
POST {{payment}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{authorizeKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "orderId": "order-1", "paymentMethod": "tok_approve", "amount": {"amountMinor": 79900, "currency": "EUR"}}

> {% client.global.set("paymentId", response.body.id); %}

### The same request with the same key: the first response again, Idempotent-Replayed: true, and nothing more is authorized
POST {{payment}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{authorizeKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "orderId": "order-1", "paymentMethod": "tok_approve", "amount": {"amountMinor": 79900, "currency": "EUR"}}

### Without a key: 400, idempotencyKeyRequired
POST {{payment}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "orderId": "order-1", "paymentMethod": "tok_approve", "amount": {"amountMinor": 79900, "currency": "EUR"}}

### The Customer reads it back with their own token
GET {{payment}}/payments/{{paymentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### The same, through the API gateway
GET {{gateway}}/payments/{{paymentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### The Customer's Payments for the Order, newest first, through the gateway
GET {{gateway}}/payments?orderId=order-1
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### The Saga voids it: 200, VOIDED, with a VOID transaction
POST {{payment}}/payments/{{paymentId}}/void
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}"}

### Voiding it again: the same 200, and nothing more is recorded
POST {{payment}}/payments/{{paymentId}}/void
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}"}

### The gateway hides the commands: 404
POST {{gateway}}/payments/{{paymentId}}/void
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}"}

### A declining test card: 201, recorded as DECLINED with its declineReason, card_declined
POST {{payment}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "orderId": "order-2", "paymentMethod": "tok_decline", "amount": {"amountMinor": 79900, "currency": "EUR"}}

> {% client.global.set("declinedPaymentId", response.body.id); %}

### The Customer reads the declined Payment back too
GET {{payment}}/payments/{{declinedPaymentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### A declined Payment can't be voided: 409, paymentNotVoidable
POST {{payment}}/payments/{{declinedPaymentId}}/void
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}"}

### Not enough funds: DECLINED, insufficient_funds
POST {{payment}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "orderId": "order-3", "paymentMethod": "tok_insufficient_funds", "amount": {"amountMinor": 79900, "currency": "EUR"}}

### A token the mock doesn't know: DECLINED, unknown_payment_method
POST {{payment}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "orderId": "order-4", "paymentMethod": "tok_visa", "amount": {"amountMinor": 79900, "currency": "EUR"}}

### The gateway fails to answer: 502, and no Payment is recorded
POST {{payment}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "orderId": "order-5", "paymentMethod": "tok_gateway_error", "amount": {"amountMinor": 79900, "currency": "EUR"}}

### No paymentMethod: 400
POST {{payment}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "orderId": "order-1", "amount": {"amountMinor": 79900, "currency": "EUR"}}

### An unknown Payment: 404
GET {{payment}}/payments/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### An amount that isn't positive: 400
POST {{payment}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "orderId": "order-1", "paymentMethod": "tok_approve", "amount": {"amountMinor": 0, "currency": "EUR"}}

### An unknown currency: 400
POST {{payment}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "orderId": "order-1", "paymentMethod": "tok_approve", "amount": {"amountMinor": 79900, "currency": "XYZ"}}

### A Customer can't authorize a payment, only Orchestration can: 403
POST {{payment}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "orderId": "order-1", "paymentMethod": "tok_approve", "amount": {"amountMinor": 79900, "currency": "EUR"}}

### Without a token: 401
POST {{payment}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "orderId": "order-1", "paymentMethod": "tok_approve", "amount": {"amountMinor": 79900, "currency": "EUR"}}

### Staff token
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=dev-cli&username=staff@ecomm.local&password=staff

> {% client.global.set("staffToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### Staff read every Payment for an Order, with its transactions, through the gateway
GET {{gateway}}/staff/payments?orderId=order-1
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### A Customer can't: 403
GET {{gateway}}/staff/payments?orderId=order-1
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Staff read Payments only under /staff/payments: 403
GET {{payment}}/payments/{{paymentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### Orchestration authorizes an Order's payment under a key of the Saga's shape: 201, AUTHORIZED
< {% client.global.set("sagaAuthorizeKey", "http-file-" + $random.uuid + ":run-1:authorizePayment"); %}
POST {{payment}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{sagaAuthorizeKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "orderId": "order-saga-1", "paymentMethod": "tok_approve", "amount": {"amountMinor": 79900, "currency": "EUR"}}

> {% client.global.set("sagaPaymentId", response.body.id); %}

### Orchestration reads it, naming the Customer, as the Saga does while it awaits settlement
GET {{payment}}/payments/{{sagaPaymentId}}?customerId={{customerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}

### Naming another Customer: 404
GET {{payment}}/payments/{{sagaPaymentId}}?customerId=someone-else
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}

### Orchestration voids it: 200, VOIDED; voiding again is the same 200
POST {{payment}}/payments/{{sagaPaymentId}}/void
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}"}

### A Customer can't read as Orchestration does: 403
GET {{payment}}/payments/{{sagaPaymentId}}?customerId={{customerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
